<treenode node="PEAR_Error;PHP:Class Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\PEAR.php;f0;830;1;1104;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    class PEAR_Error&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Standard PEAR error class for PHP 4&#10;This class is supserseded by {&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: PEAR_Exception} in PHP 5&#10;&lt;b&gt;category&lt;/b&gt;: pear&#10;&lt;b&gt;package&lt;/b&gt;: PEAR&#10;&lt;b&gt;author&lt;/b&gt;: Stig Bakken &lt;ssb&#10;&lt;b&gt;php&lt;/b&gt;: .net&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;author&lt;/b&gt;: Tomas V.V. Cox &lt;cox&#10;&lt;b&gt;idecnet&lt;/b&gt;: .com&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;author&lt;/b&gt;: Gregory Beaver &lt;cellog&#10;&lt;b&gt;php&lt;/b&gt;: .net&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;copyright&lt;/b&gt;: 1997-2006 The PHP Group&#10;&lt;b&gt;license&lt;/b&gt;: http://opensource.org/licenses/bsd-license.php New BSD License&#10;&lt;b&gt;version&lt;/b&gt;: Release: 1.10.7&#10;&lt;b&gt;link&lt;/b&gt;: http://pear.php.net/manual/en/core.pear.pear-error.php&#10;&lt;b&gt;see&lt;/b&gt;: PEAR::raiseError(), PEAR::throwError()&#10;&lt;b&gt;since&lt;/b&gt;: Class available since PHP 4.0.2;;d0,831;;b0,0;;m0;;e">
<treenode node="PEAR_Error;PHP:Function Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\PEAR.php;f11;941;5;946;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    PEAR_Error(&#10;        $message = &apos;unknown error&apos;, $code = null, $mode = null,&#10;        $options = null, $userinfo = null&#10;    )&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Only here for backwards compatibility.&#10;Class &quot;Cache_Error&quot; still uses it, among others.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$message&lt;/b&gt;: Message&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$code&lt;/b&gt;: Error code&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$mode&lt;/b&gt;: Error mode&#10;    mixed &lt;b&gt;$options&lt;/b&gt;: See __construct()&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$userinfo&lt;/b&gt;: Additional user/debug info;;d6,944;;b1,0;;m0;;estring $message;;pint $code;;pint $mode;;pmixed $options;;pstring $userinfo;;p">
</treenode>
<treenode node="__construct;PHP:Function Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\PEAR.php;f4;860;5;928;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    __construct($message = &apos;unknown error&apos;, $code = null,&#10;                        $mode = null, $options = null, $userinfo = null)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    PEAR_Error constructor&#10;&lt;b&gt;access&lt;/b&gt;: public&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$message&lt;/b&gt;: message&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$code&lt;/b&gt;: (optional) error code&#10;    int &lt;b&gt;$mode&lt;/b&gt;: (optional) error mode, one of: PEAR_ERROR_RETURN, PEAR_ERROR_PRINT, PEAR_ERROR_DIE, PEAR_ERROR_TRIGGER, PEAR_ERROR_CALLBACK or PEAR_ERROR_EXCEPTION&#10;    mixed &lt;b&gt;$options&lt;/b&gt;: (optional) error level, _OR_ in the case of PEAR_ERROR_CALLBACK, the callback function or object/method tuple.&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$userinfo&lt;/b&gt;: (optional) additional user/debug info;;d4,862;;b0,0;;m0;;estring $message;;pint $code;;pint $mode;;pmixed $options;;pstring $userinfo;;p">
</treenode>
