</treenode>
<treenode node="parseHelloFields;PHP:Function Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\SMTP.php;f14;768;5;802;;;;vpos;;v;;a;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    parseHelloFields($type)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Parse a reply to HELO/EHLO command to discover server extensions.&#10;In case of HELO, the only parameter that can be discovered is a server name.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$type&lt;/b&gt;: `HELO` or `EHLO`;;d4,769;;b2,0;;m0;;estring $type;;p">
</treenode>
<treenode node="quit;PHP:Function Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\SMTP.php;f11;836;5;846;;;;vpos;;v;;abool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    quit($close_on_error = true)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Send an SMTP QUIT command.&#10;Closes the socket if there is no error or the $close_on_error argument is true.&#10;Implements from RFC 821: QUIT &lt;CRLF&gt;.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    bool &lt;b&gt;$close_on_error&lt;/b&gt;: Should the connection close if an error occurs?;;d4,837;;b1,0;;m0;;ebool $close_on_error;;p">
</treenode>
<treenode node="recipient;PHP:Function Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\SMTP.php;f11;858;5;865;;;;vpos;;v;;abool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    recipient($address)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Send an SMTP RCPT command.&#10;Sets the TO argument to $toaddr.&#10;Returns true if the recipient was accepted false if it was rejected.&#10;Implements from RFC 821: RCPT &lt;SP&gt; TO:&lt;forward-path&gt; &lt;CRLF&gt;.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$address&lt;/b&gt;: The address the message is being sent to;;d4,859;;b1,0;;m0;;estring $address;;p">
</treenode>
<treenode node="recordLastTransactionID;PHP:Function Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\SMTP.php;f14;1293;5;1310;;;;vpos;;v;;abool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    recordLastTransactionID()&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Extract and return the ID of the last SMTP transaction based on&#10;a list of patterns provided in SMTP::$smtp_transaction_id_patterns.&#10;Relies on the host providing the ID in response to a DATA command.&#10;If no reply has been received yet, it will return null.&#10;If no pattern was matched, it will return false.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   |null|string;;d4,1294;;b2,0;;m0;;e">
</treenode>
<treenode node="reset;PHP:Function Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\SMTP.php;f11;874;5;877;;;;vpos;;v;;abool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    reset()&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Send an SMTP RSET command.&#10;Abort any transaction that is currently in progress.&#10;Implements RFC 821: RSET &lt;CRLF&gt;.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   True on success;;d4,875;;b1,0;;m0;;e">
</treenode>
<treenode node="sendAndMail;PHP:Function Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\SMTP.php;f11;959;5;962;;;;vpos;;v;;abool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    sendAndMail($from)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Send an SMTP SAML command.&#10;Starts a mail transaction from the email address specified in $from.&#10;Returns true if successful or false otherwise. If True&#10;the mail transaction is started and then one or more recipient&#10;commands may be called followed by a data command. This command&#10;will send the message to the users terminal if they are logged&#10;in and send them an email.&#10;Implements RFC 821: SAML &lt;SP&gt; FROM:&lt;reverse-path&gt; &lt;CRLF&gt;.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$from&lt;/b&gt;: The address the message is from;;d4,960;;b1,0;;m0;;estring $from;;p">
</treenode>
<treenode node="sendCommand;PHP:Function Name;C:\xampp\htdocs\varunika\Mail\SMTP.php;f14;888;5;943;;;;vpos;;v;;abool;;r&#10;&lt;b&gt;Definition&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    sendCommand($command, $commandstring, $expect)&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Description&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    Send a command to an SMTP server and check its return code.&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Parameters:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$command&lt;/b&gt;: The command name - not sent to the server&#10;    string &lt;b&gt;$commandstring&lt;/b&gt;: The actual command to send&#10;    int|array &lt;b&gt;$expect&lt;/b&gt;: One or more expected integer success codes&#10;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Return:&lt;/b&gt;&#10;   True on success;;d4,889;;b2,0;;m0;;estring $command;;pstring $commandstring;;pint|array $expect;;p">
</treenode>
